    <node id="DECLARATION OF INDEPENDENCE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Declaration of Independence is the foundational American document that proclaimed the thirteen colonies' separation from British rule. It served as a direct inspiration for the Patriotes, a group who adopted its resolutions and language, drawing explicit parallels between their own struggle and that of the American colonies. The document is also historically notable for being signed by Lyman Hall, one of the three delegates from Georgia. Thus, the Declaration of Independence functions both as a universal symbol of revolutionary ideals and as a specific artifact bearing the signatures of its individual signatories, including Hall.
Relationships:
  - Source: PATRIOTES
  - Target: DECLARATION OF INDEPENDENCE
  - Description: The Patriotes' resolutions recalled the language of the Declaration of Independence.</data>
