    <node id="DALHOUSIE">
      <data key="d3">5</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Dalhousie, also known as Lord Dalhousie, served as a governor of Lower Canada (and later of Canada) during a period of significant political tension. He was a governor who was initially disposed to be friendly, yet he faced the challenging and confrontational attitude of Louis-Joseph Papineau, a prominent political figure. Dalhousie's policies came under direct attack from Papineau, who criticized his governance and administrative decisions. Under Dalhousie's regime, Papineau and John Neilson worked together, forming a political alliance in opposition to the governor's measures. Despite his initial inclination toward amicable relations, Dalhousie's tenure was marked by conflict with Papineau, leading to a strained and contentious political environment in the colony.
Relationships: None listed</data>
