    <node id="LOUIS JOSEPH PAPINEAU">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Louis Joseph Papineau was a prominent French-Canadian political figure and the leader of the rebellion, as referenced in chapter titles and illustrations. He served as Speaker of the Assembly for over two decades, a role he assumed in 1815 after first entering the House of Assembly in 1812. Papineau led the Patriote party, advocating for French-Canadian rights and opposing British colonial policies, including the proposed union of Upper and Lower Canada in 1822. His leadership continued until the rebellion of 1837, which he spearheaded.
Relationships: None listed</data>
