    <node id="IT WAS A SHORT-LIVED REVOLT, LASTING SCARCELY A WEEK, AND WAS LED BY ROBERT NELSON ALONGSIDE OTHER PATRIOT LEADERS. THE REBELLION AIMED TO CHALLENGE BRITISH COLONIAL AUTHORITY AND PUSH FOR POLITICAL REFORMS, BUT IT ENDED IN DECISIVE DEFEAT AND WAS QUICKLY SUPPRESSED BY GOVERNMENT FORCES. DESPITE ITS BRIEF DURATION, THE EVENT MARKED A SIGNIFICANT MOMENT IN THE STRUGGLE FOR RESPONSIBLE GOVERNMENT IN THE CANADIAN COLONIES, ULTIMATELY CONTRIBUTING TO BROADER POLITICAL CHANGES IN THE REGION.">
