    <node id="LAFONTAINE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">LaFontaine was a prominent rebel leader and political figure in Canadian history. He went abroad after the rebellion, having first attempted to persuade Governor Gosford to call the legislature as a means of addressing grievances. As an old lieutenant of Louis-Joseph Papineau, LaFontaine played a crucial role in making possible Papineau’s eventual return to Canada. However, their relationship later deteriorated into an open breach, marking a significant political rupture between the two men.
Relationships: None specified in the data.</data>
