    <node id="DAVIGNON">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">DAVIGNON was a French Canadian individual who became involved in the rebellion led by the Patriotes. He was arrested by British troopers for his participation in the uprising, marking him as a rebel in the eyes of the colonial authorities. However, his imprisonment was short-lived, as he was later liberated by the Patriotes themselves. The rescue operation that freed him was led by Dr. Kimber, a figure associated with the rebellion, which further confirms Davignon’s active role in the insurgency. His arrest and subsequent liberation highlight his direct engagement with the rebel cause, as well as the coordinated efforts of the Patriotes to recover their captured members. Davignon’s story reflects the broader tensions and conflicts of the period, where French Canadians rose against British rule, and his experience underscores the personal risks and collective actions taken by those involved in the rebellion.
Relationships:
  - Source: DAVIGNON
  - Target: PATRIOTES
  - Description: The Patriotes liberated Davignon from British custody

  - Source: LIEUTENANT ERMATINGER
  - Target: DAVIGNON
  - Description: Lieutenant Ermatinger arrested Davignon

  - Source: DR KIMBER
  - Target: DAVIGNON
  - Description: Dr Kimber was a ringleader in the rescue of Davignon.</data>
