    <node id="HE WAS PRESENT AT THE BATTLE OF ST. DENIS BUT LEFT EARLY FOR ST. HYACINTHE, AND AFTER THE DEFEAT AT ST. CHARLES, HE FLED TO THE VERMONT BORDER AND EVENTUALLY TO THE UNITED STATES. HE HAD PRIOR MILITARY EXPERIENCE AS A MILITIA MAJOR, WHICH INFORMED HIS ROLE IN THE CONFLICT.">
