    <node id="THIS UPRISING WAS DRIVEN BY THE PATRIOTES' DEMANDS FOR DEMOCRATIC REFORMS, GREATER LOCAL AUTONOMY, AND RESISTANCE TO THE BRITISH COLONIAL GOVERNMENT'S AUTHORITARIAN RULE. THE PARTY'S LEADERSHIP, PARTICULARLY PAPINEAU, PLAYED A CENTRAL ROLE IN ORGANIZING AND INSPIRING THE REBELLION, WHICH ULTIMATELY FAILED BUT SIGNIFICANTLY INFLUENCED CANADIAN POLITICAL DEVELOPMENT. THE PATRIOTE PARTY'S ACTIONS AND IDEOLOGY WERE INSEPARABLE FROM THE REBELLION, AS THEY SOUGHT TO ADDRESS GRIEVANCES THROUGH BOTH POLITICAL AGITATION AND, ULTIMATELY, ARMED RESISTANCE.">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Papineau led the Patriote party until the outbreak of rebellion in 1837, which he was associated with. Papineau led the Patriote party until the outbreak of rebellion, and he was a key figure in the rebellion.</data>
