  - Description: Robert Bouchette was a rebel leader associated with the Rebellion, a movement or uprising in which he played a significant role. He was captured during or after the rebellion and subsequently held as a political prisoner. As part of his punishment, Bouchette was transported to Bermuda, where he was sent into exile or penal servitude. These details indicate that he was both a prominent figure in the rebellion and a victim of its consequences, facing imprisonment and forced relocation.

  - Source: GIROD
