    <node id="CAPTAIN">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Based on the provided descriptions, the entity "CAPTAIN" refers to a complex and multifaceted character who appears in various narratives, embodying different roles and experiences.

Primarily, the Captain is a seasoned mariner. He is a ship's captain who has sailed to distant locations such as China and Bombay, having previously worked on the Anchor Line. He is described as an "awfully good man" of Scottish origin. His maritime career has been marked by tragedy; his vessel once wrecked on the Brisons, an event in which he survived but his wife drowned. In another instance, he is the captain of a boat grieving the loss of a friend, expressing regret about his own life and money. Despite a gruff exterior, he shows gentleness toward a character named Miss Drake.

Beyond his nautical life, the Captain appears in other contexts. He is a leader who warns about "pung-dongs" and is counted among the defenders in a particular conflict. He also plays a jest on characters named Selmann and Tobias, and is mentioned as making a "sentimental journey through the stables." Additionally, he observed that alcohol did not strengthen his sailors, suggesting a pragmatic and observational nature.

Overall, the Captain is a resilient, experienced, and somewhat tragic figure, defined by his seafaring past, personal losses, and a blend of sternness and underlying compassion.
Relationships: None listed.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
