    <node id="PIONEER HOOK AND LADDER COMPANY">
      <data key="d3">1</data>
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Pioneer Hook and Ladder Company is a historic fire company based in St. Paul, Minnesota. It is recognized as a fire company that has participated in parades, and it holds a notable place in the history of the St. Paul Fire Department. The company is specifically mentioned in historical records of the department, indicating its role in the development and operations of firefighting services in the city. As a hook and ladder company, it would have been responsible for providing ladder and rescue services, as well as handling equipment for accessing upper floors of buildings. Its inclusion in parade events suggests it has been an active and visible participant in community and civic celebrations, reflecting its longstanding presence and service within St. Paul. Overall, Pioneer Hook and Ladder Company represents a traditional and integral part of the city's firefighting heritage, contributing to both emergency response and public engagement throughout its history.
Relationships:
  - Source: FIRE DEPARTMENT
  - Target: PIONEER HOOK AND LADDER COMPANY
  - Description: The Pioneer Hook and Ladder company was part of the fire department</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
