    <node id="FIRE ENGINE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A fire engine is a specialized machine designed for extinguishing fires, with its development rooted in historical advancements across Europe and the United States. These vehicles have evolved significantly over time, incorporating pumps, water tanks, hoses, and other firefighting equipment to combat blazes effectively. In practical application, fire engines have been essential in urban firefighting efforts. For instance, the first fire engine purchased by McCloud and Ritchie was deployed to fight fires in St. Paul, marking a key milestone in the city's firefighting history. This early adoption highlights the critical role fire engines played in protecting communities and shaping modern fire response systems.
Relationships:
  - Source: FIREMEN
  - Target: FIRE ENGINE
  - Description: Firemen used fire engines in their work.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: NEW YORK
  - Description: Fire engines were used in New York.
  - Source: ENGLAND
  - Target: FIRE ENGINE
  - Description: An improved fire engine was patented in England in the late seventeenth century.
  - Source: PARIS
  - Target: FIRE ENGINE
  - Description: The oldest record of a fire engine was found in Paris in 1684.
  - Source: PIONEER HOOK AND LADDER COMPANY NO. 1
  - Target: FIRE ENGINE
  - Description: The company possessed one fire engine with hose.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: SUCTION PIPE
  - Description: Early fire engines had a suction pipe of strong leather.
  - Source: AMSTERDAM
  - Target: FIRE ENGINE
  - Description: Leather hose and suction pipe were introduced in Amsterdam, used in fire engines.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: CISTERN
  - Description: Early fire engines used a cistern of oak placed on wheels.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: PUMP
  - Description: Early fire engines were furnished with a pump.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: AIR CHAMBER
  - Description: Early fire engines had an air chamber to throw water to a great height.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: SPIRAL PIECE OF METAL
  - Description: The fire engine's suction pipe contained a spiral piece of metal.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: KING'S LIBRARY
  - Description: The oldest fire engine was used in the king's library.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: FIRE LADDIES
  - Description: Fire laddies used early fire engines.
  - Source: FIRE ENGINE
  - Target: DOUBLE-DECK HAND FIRE ENGINES
  - Description: Double-deck hand fire engines are a type of fire engine.</data>
