    <node id="THEIR ACTIONS RANGED FROM ORGANIZED MILITARY ENGAGEMENTS TO CONTROVERSIAL IRREGULAR OPERATIONS, AND THEY WERE INSTRUMENTAL IN DEFEATING REBEL FORCES AT SEVERAL KEY LOCATIONS. THE LOYALIST MILITARY PRESENCE INCLUDED REGULAR BRITISH TROOPS, LOCALLY RAISED MILITIA COMPANIES, AND VOLUNTEER CORPS, EACH CONTRIBUTING TO THE EVENTUAL SUPPRESSION OF THE REBELLION [DATA: ENTITIES (9127, 9184, 9097); RELATIONSHIPS (14233, 14229, 14239)].">
