ENTITY: AMERICAN COLONIES
Description: The American colonies were a group of thirteen British settlements along the eastern coast of North America that revolted in 1775, sparking the American Revolution. These colonies—often referred to collectively as the thirteen colonies—were the historical entities whose revolutionary methods, such as boycotting English goods, served as a direct inspiration for later movements, notably the Patriotes in Canada. Their rebellion against British rule was characterized by organized resistance, including economic non-cooperation, which became a model for other groups seeking political change. The colonies' successful fight for independence established them as a foundational example of colonial self-determination and revolutionary action.
