    <node id="FIRST REGIMENT">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">FIRST REGIMENT was a military unit to which Berdan's sharpshooters were attached, indicating its role in specialized light infantry and marksmanship operations during the American Civil War. The regiment also served as the home unit for Capt. Henry C. Coates, who initially held the rank of lieutenant within its ranks and later rose to command the regiment. Coates’s service with the FIRST REGIMENT included participation in battles up to and including the Battle of Gettysburg, marking the unit’s involvement in significant engagements of the Eastern Theater. The regiment thus combined the elite sharpshooter corps with regular line infantry duties, and its leadership under Coates reflected a progression from junior officer to regimental commander, with combat experience culminating at Gettysburg.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.

