      <data key="d4">ENTITY: SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN SUPPLEMENT
Description: Scientific American Supplement was a weekly publication that served as a supplement to the long-established Scientific American magazine, which was founded in 1845. As part of the Scientific American family of publications, this supplement was dedicated to covering a broad range of scientific topics, offering readers in-depth articles and papers on contemporary scientific developments. The publication functioned as a weekly periodical, and in addition to its regular content, it provided a catalogue of scientific papers, making it a valuable resource for those seeking both current research and a curated list of related scholarly works. The supplement published original scientific papers and contributed to the dissemination of scientific knowledge within the broader Scientific American framework.
