    <node id="MR. GLADSTONE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Mr. Gladstone, a prominent British political figure, is identified as William Ewart Gladstone, a leading statesman of the Victorian era. He is referenced in multiple contexts, including his involvement in the election in Midlothian, where he campaigned vigorously, and his role as a political leader who introduced the Home Rule Bill of 1893. This bill, which sought to grant Ireland self-governance, was a central topic in parliamentary debates. Mr. Gladstone is also confirmed to be the same individual as Gladstone, the British Prime Minister, and his political career is discussed in relation to Home Rule and other significant issues of his time. His legacy is marked by his leadership, legislative initiatives, and enduring impact on British politics.
Relationships:
  - Source: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Target: HOME RULE BILL OF 1893
  - Description: Mr. Gladstone introduced the Home Rule Bill, making him the primary proponent; Mr. Gladstone introduced the Home Rule Bill of 1893, making him the primary proponent.
  - Source: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Target: HOME RULE
  - Description: Mr. Gladstone is the leader who introduced the Home Rule Bill, making him a central figure in the movement.
  - Source: ELSIE
  - Target: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Description: Elsie comments on Mr. Gladstone's Home Rule Bill, showing her engagement with his policies; Elsie comments on Mr. Gladstone's bill, showing her engagement with his policies.
  - Source: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Target: WOMAN'S SUFFRAGE
  - Description: Mr. Gladstone's Liberal Party did not grant women the vote, indicating a weak relationship with suffrage.
  - Source: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Target: FRANCHISE
  - Description: Mr. Gladstone's Liberal Party did not grant women the vote, indicating a weak relationship with the franchise.
  - Source: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Target: PARLIAMENT
  - Description: Mr. Gladstone introduced the Home Rule Bill in Parliament, making him a key figure in the debate; Mr. Gladstone's Home Rule Bill was debated in Parliament, where obstructive talk occurred.
  - Source: MR. GLADSTONE
  - Target: MIDLOTHIAN
  - Description: Mr. Gladstone is contesting an election in Midlothian, indicating a political candidacy relationship</data>
