      <data key="d1">William F. Russel was a compositor (a typesetter) working for the Pioneer newspaper. In addition to his trade, he took on a military initiative by organizing a company of sharpshooters in St. Paul. This group was formed as a volunteer unit, reflecting his leadership and civic engagement during a period of conflict. His dual role as a skilled print worker and a military organizer highlights his diverse contributions to his community.
