ENTITY: GLADSTONE, W. E.
Description: W. E. Gladstone was a British politician who is historically noted for his support of the Russell Resolutions, a set of legislative measures that were actively opposed by the Patriotes, a political group in Lower Canada. His backing of these resolutions placed him in direct opposition to the Patriotes' demands for greater self-governance and reform. Gladstone's political stance on this issue reflects his broader engagement with colonial and constitutional matters during his career in British politics.
