    <node id="BEY OF THE CAMP">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The "Bey of the Camp" is a title held by Sidi Mohammed, a leader or official within the camp who holds administrative authority in the Jereed region. This role encompasses the management of camp affairs, including the collection of tribute from the local palm-groves. As a tribute collector, the Bey of the Camp is responsible for gathering payments or levies from the palm-grove owners and cultivators in El-Jereed. Additionally, the title includes the duty of overseeing water transport, indicating a broader logistical and resource-management function within the camp. Sidi Mohammed, as the Bey of the Camp, thus serves as a key administrative and fiscal figure, combining leadership, tribute collection, and water-related responsibilities in the Jereed area.
Relationships:
