    <node id="THE BEY'S PRESENTS">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Bey's Presents refer to the gifts or offerings presented by the Bey, a local ruler or high-ranking official, typically in the context of diplomatic exchanges or as tokens of respect to visiting dignitaries. These presents are explicitly mentioned in the source text as formal gifts given by the Bey, underscoring their role in ceremonial or political interactions. The term encompasses both the act of giving and the material items themselves, which would have been selected to convey goodwill, honor, or alliance. While the specific contents of these presents are not detailed, their mention highlights the Bey's authority and the importance of gift-giving in maintaining social and political relationships. The Bey's presents thus serve as a symbol of the ruler's generosity and the formal protocols surrounding his court.
