    <node id="DURING THE ASSAULT, THE REGIMENT FORMED UP ON ONE SIDE OF THE CHURCH, ALONGSIDE THE 83RD REGIMENT, AS THE REBELS WERE DRIVEN OUT [DATA: ENTITIES (9168, 9183); RELATIONSHIPS (13902, 13930, 13998); SOURCES (427, 428)].">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Sir John Colborne commanded the 32nd regiment as part of his column
