      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
      <data key="d4">
The engagement at St. Eustache was the final major battle of the Lower Canada Rebellion. The regiment's participation is documented in the context of Sir John Colborne's column, which also included the 1st Royals, the 83rd Regiment, the Montreal Volunteer Rifles, and other forces, totaling over two thousand men [Data: Sources (427)].

The data does not provide specific dates or locations for any other battles involving the 32nd Regiment beyond the engagement at St. Eustache in December 1837.

---

