    <node id="BATTLE OF SHILOH">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Battle of Shiloh, also known as the Battle of Pittsburg Landing, was a major engagement of the American Civil War. The alternative name derives from a small church located near the battlefield, which served as a prominent landmark. The battle took place along the Tennessee River, where Union and Confederate forces clashed in intense fighting. It was characterized by significant casualties on both sides, and the arrival of reinforcements played a crucial role in the outcome. The engagement is a central event in the historical narrative, highlighting the brutal nature of the conflict and the strategic importance of the riverine position.
Relationships: (None provided in the data)

---</data>
