    <node id="THIS MOVEMENT WAS PART OF THE BATTALION'S OPERATIONAL DEPLOYMENT DURING THE AMERICAN CIVIL WAR, AS IT WAS DIRECTED TO REINFORCE OR SUPPORT THE GARRISON AT THE FORT. THE ORDER, ISSUED IN THAT MONTH, PLACED THE BATTALION AT FORT HENRY, A KEY CONFEDERATE STRONGHOLD ON THE TENNESSEE RIVER, WHICH WAS STRATEGICALLY IMPORTANT FOR CONTROLLING RIVER TRAFFIC AND REGIONAL SUPPLY LINES. THE BATTALION'S ARRIVAL AT FORT HENRY OCCURRED IN THE CONTEXT OF THE BROADER UNION CAMPAIGN TO CAPTURE THE FORT, WHICH ULTIMATELY FELL TO UNION FORCES LATER THAT SAME MONTH. NO FURTHER DETAILS ARE PROVIDED REGARDING THE BATTALION'S SPECIFIC ACTIONS, STRENGTH, OR SUBSEQUENT MOVEMENTS, BUT THE ORDER TO FORT HENRY IN FEBRUARY 1862 IS THE SOLE DOCUMENTED EVENT IN THIS SUMMARY.">
