    <node id="IT WAS RECENTLY PAROLED—MEANING ITS SOLDIERS HAD BEEN RELEASED FROM CAPTIVITY OR FROM A PRIOR SURRENDER—AND SUBSEQUENTLY PARTICIPATED IN TWO SIGNIFICANT MILITARY ACTIONS: GENERAL HENRY H. SIBLEY’S EXPEDITION AND THE BATTLE OF WOOD LAKE. THE BATTLE OF WOOD LAKE, FOUGHT ON SEPTEMBER 23, 1862, WAS A DECISIVE ENGAGEMENT IN WHICH SIBLEY’S FORCES DEFEATED A LARGE DAKOTA FORCE, EFFECTIVELY ENDING THE MAJOR HOSTILITIES OF THE CONFLICT IN MINNESOTA. THE REGIMENT’S INVOLVEMENT IN THIS BATTLE AND IN SIBLEY’S BROADER CAMPAIGN UNDERSCORES ITS ACTIVE COMBAT ROLE DURING THIS PERIOD.">
