**ENTITY: FIRST MINNESOTA BATTERY**
Description: The First Minnesota Battery was a Union light artillery unit organized at Fort Snelling in 1861. It was the only Minnesota military organization present at the Battle of Pittsburg Landing (also known as the Battle of Shiloh), where it performed gallantly in action. Beyond this engagement, the battery also participated in the battles of Vicksburg and Atlanta, as well as General Sherman's march to the sea. The unit's service spanned several major campaigns of the Western Theater, and it was distinguished by its bravery and effectiveness as an artillery force throughout the war.
