      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Melilla is a city located on the Mediterranean coast of Morocco, specifically on the Moroccan shore of the Mediterranean Sea. It is historically an ancient settlement, originally founded by the Carthaginians, and is mentioned in various lists of coastal towns. Over time, Melilla became a Spanish presidio (a fortified military outpost) and serves as the capital of the province of Garet. The city's population is approximately 3,000 residents. Despite its geographical position on the African continent, Melilla remains under Spanish sovereignty, functioning as an autonomous city of Spain. Its dual heritage—rooted in ancient Carthaginian origins and later Spanish military and administrative control—shapes its unique cultural and political identity.
