    <node id="CERTIFICATE OF DEPOSIT">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">A certificate of deposit (CD) is a financial document representing a sum of twenty thousand dollars held in a western bank. This specific certificate was presented at the bank by an individual named Simon, accompanied by his party. The document itself names the bank where the funds are deposited, and it forms part of the official papers belonging to John A. Lasco. Thus, the certificate serves as both a record of the deposited amount and a piece of evidence within Lasco's financial or legal documentation.
Relationships:
  - Source: JOHN A. LASCO
  - Target: CERTIFICATE OF DEPOSIT
  - Description: The certificate of deposit is part of his papers. The certificate of deposit is part of John A. Lasco's papers, naming the bank with the twenty thousand dollars.
  - Source: TWENTY THOUSAND DOLLARS
  - Target: CERTIFICATE OF DEPOSIT
  - Description: The certificate of deposit names the bank where the twenty thousand dollars is deposited.</data>
