    <node id="AUNT ELSIE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">Aunt Elsie is the affectionate family nickname for Dr. Elsie Inglis, a figure known both for her professional achievements and her personal warmth. To her nieces and young relatives, she was a beloved aunt who was appreciated for her thoughtful gifts and her engaging companionship. Within the context of a family crisis, Aunt Elsie is also described as a relative of a dying woman, actively involved in her care and in making the necessary arrangements. She helped manage the household during the illness, demonstrating her practical support and dedication to family duties.

Beyond her role as a caring aunt and caregiver, Aunt Elsie is confirmed to be the same person as Elsie Inglis. She was a skilled needlewoman, a talent she likely shared with her family, and she was also a passionate advocate for women's causes. This combination of domestic skill, familial devotion, and public advocacy paints a picture of a multifaceted individual who balanced her professional and personal life with grace. Her identity as "Aunt Elsie" highlights the personal, affectionate side of a woman who was also a prominent figure in her field, showing that her legacy included both her public work and her private kindness to those closest to her.
Relationships: (No explicit relationships listed in the data tables for this entity.)

