    <node id="NICTE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">NICTE, also known as Zuhuy-Kuk, is a significant figure in Maya mythology and history. She is described as a priestess and the daughter of CAN and COZ, making her part of a prominent lineage. NICTE is revered as the goddess of maidens and is counted among the seven founders of her cultural or religious tradition. Her role extends beyond divine association; she was also the sister of Chaacmol and assisted her brother Cay, who served as the pontiff, in the sanctuary. Her connection to sacred duties is further evidenced by her association with inscriptions found at Uxmal, an important Maya archaeological site. Thus, NICTE embodies both mythological and historical importance, blending divine attributes with active priestly service within her community.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
