      <data key="d1">Kinich-Kakmo is the deified name of Moo, a figure who received apotheosis honors and had temples raised in her memory at Izamal. She is also identified as a deified daughter of CAN, worshiped at a shrine in Mayab, where people came to hear oracles. The name Kinich-Kakmo translates to "fiery macaw with eyes like the sun," under which Moo was worshiped in Izamal.
