    <node id="HE IS BEST KNOWN FOR HIS CONCILIATORY POLICY AND GENIAL DEMEANOR, WHICH HE ATTEMPTED TO APPLY IN GOVERNING THE COLONY DURING A PERIOD OF RISING POLITICAL TENSION. AS PART OF HIS EFFORTS TO MAINTAIN ORDER, HE ISSUED A PROCLAMATION ON JUNE 15, 1837, CALLING ON LOYAL SUBJECTS TO DISCOUNTENANCE SEDITIOUS WRITINGS AND AVOID TURBULENT MEETINGS. HOWEVER, HIS POLICY OF CONCILIATION ULTIMATELY FAILED TO QUELL THE GROWING UNREST, LEADING HIM TO RECOMMEND HIS OWN RESIGNATION. HIS TENURE THUS ENDED IN 1838, MARKING THE CLOSE OF AN ADMINISTRATION DEFINED BY AN INITIAL ATTEMPT AT PEACEFUL GOVERNANCE THAT PROVED UNSUCCESSFUL IN THE FACE OF ESCALATING CONFLICT.">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
