    <node id="SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN is a distinguished scientific journal that was established in 1845, making it one of the oldest continuously published periodicals of its kind. As a scientific publication, it is known for its in-depth coverage of research, discoveries, and developments across various fields of science and technology. The journal is published in conjunction with the SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN SUPPLEMENT, a companion publication that offers combined subscription rates to readers. This arrangement allows subscribers to access both the main journal and the supplement as a single, integrated package, providing a broader range of scientific content and analysis. Together, these publications serve as a comprehensive resource for scientists, educators, and the general public interested in staying informed about scientific progress and its implications for society.
Relationships:
  - Source: SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN SUPPLEMENT
  - Target: SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN
  - Description: Scientific American Supplement is a supplementary publication issued in conjunction with the main periodical, Scientific American. The two are published together, and they are offered to subscribers at a combined subscription rate, meaning that the Supplement is not sold separately but as part of a bundled subscription with its parent magazine. As a supplement, it extends the content and coverage of Scientific American, providing additional material to readers who subscribe to both. The relationship is integral: the Supplement exists solely as an adjunct to Scientific American, and the combined offering reflects their shared publication and subscription structure.
  - Source: SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN
  - Target: MUNN &amp; CO.
  - Description: Munn &amp; Co. is the publisher of the Scientific American</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">2</data>
