    <node id="THE INTERNET ARCHIVE">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Internet Archive is a digital library and nonprofit organization that played a crucial role in the creation of the referenced text by supplying the necessary visual source material. Specifically, the organization provided scan images of the play in question, which were then used for transcription purposes. These posted scans served as the foundational documents from which the text was accurately reproduced, ensuring that the original content was preserved and made accessible for scholarly or editorial work. As an entity, the Internet Archive operates with a mission to provide universal access to knowledge, and its contribution here underscores its function as a vital repository for historical and literary materials. By making these images available, the organization enabled the transcription process to proceed with fidelity to the original source, thereby supporting the production and dissemination of the text.
Relationships:
  - Source: ONLINE DISTRIBUTED PROOFREADING TEAM
  - Target: THE INTERNET ARCHIVE
  - Description: The Online Distributed Proofreading Team used images from The Internet Archive to produce the text
