      <data key="d1">Sir William Muir was a prominent figure associated with the University of Edinburgh, known for his active support of the women's medical degree cause. He likely held a position as a university official or senator, using his influence to advocate for the admission of women to medical studies. Beyond his academic and administrative roles, Muir was personally connected to key individuals in the movement: he was the grandfather of Miss Arbuthnot, and he was a close friend of John Inglis, another supporter of the cause. His dual roles—both as an institutional figure and as a personal ally—underscore his commitment to advancing women's access to medical education.

