    <node id="MUTINY">
      <data key="d0">extracted</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mutiny, also known as the Indian Rebellion of 1857, was a major uprising against British rule in India. This event directly involved John Inglis, who was recalled to India specifically to participate in its suppression. During the conflict, Inglis fought alongside John Lawrence, a prominent British administrator and military leader. Together, they worked to quell the rebellion, which had spread across large parts of northern and central India. The Mutiny marked a significant turning point in British colonial history, leading to the end of the East India Company's rule and the establishment of direct British Crown control over India. John Inglis's role in this suppression, alongside John Lawrence, underscores his active military service during this turbulent period. The rebellion, though ultimately unsuccessful, had profound and lasting effects on British policy, military organization, and Indian society.
Relationships: None listed in the data.</data>
      <data key="d2">1</data>
      <data key="d3">0</data>
