    <edge source="RUDOLPH" target="CAPTAIN KNEEBONE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Rudolph and Captain Kneebone share a professional, hierarchical relationship aboard the lowdah, where they work together during an attack. Captain Kneebone holds a position of authority over Rudolph, giving him direct orders and directing his actions in battle. Rudolph is subordinate to Captain Kneebone, and their interactions reflect this chain of command. For instance, Captain Kneebone claps Rudolph on the arm and coordinates the banquet with him, a gesture that suggests both camaraderie and a superior-subordinate dynamic. Rudolph is visibly affected by Captain Kneebones praise, indicating that he values the captains approval and respects his leadership. Additionally, Rudolph accompanies Heywood to see Captain Kneebone, which further establishes that Rudolph is acquainted with the captain and has a standing relationship with him, likely as a trusted crew member or officer under his command. Their cooperation during the attack underscores a functional team dynamic, where Rudolph follows Captain Kneebones strategic direction. Overall, the relationship is defined by clear military or nautical hierarchy, mutual respect, and collaborative effort in a combat or operational setting.</data>
      <data key="d8">CAPTAIN KNEEBONE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RUDOLPH" target="KNEEBONE" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Rudolph is ordered to report to Kneebone at the northeast corner, showing a chain of command.</data>
      <data key="d8">CAPTAIN KNEEBONE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="RUDOLPH" target="NESBIT" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Rudolph and Nesbit are fellow defenders who share a history of combat and hardship, as evidenced by their physical injuriesNesbit bears a cut on his forehead, while Rudolph has a bandaged arm. Their bond is further underscored by a particularly difficult drunken dinner they endured together, which suggests a level of familiarity and shared experience beyond mere duty. Nesbit is consistently concerned for Rudolphs well-being: he attempts to restrain Rudolph during a quarrel, clearly trying to prevent escalation or harm, and he comes running immediately upon seeing Rudolph as a bloody victim, indicating a protective instinct. Their relationship is that of close acquaintances, with Nesbit often present during conversations and offering commentary on unfolding situations. Rudolph, for his part, is acutely aware of Nesbits presence and actions, recognizing his voice and trusting him as a fellow defender. Despite the tension of a quarrellikely stemming from the stress of their shared circumstancesNesbits actions reveal a deep, unspoken loyalty and a desire to keep Rudolph safe. Together, they represent a pair of comrades bound by mutual awareness, concern, and the scars of their shared service.</data>
      <data key="d8">NESBIT</data>
    </edge>
