    <edge source="PATRIOTES" target="ST CHARLES" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Patriotes, a group active in the Lower Canada Rebellion, used St Charles as a central hub for both organizational meetings and military engagements. At St Charles, they convened to plan their actions, but it was also the site of a decisive battle where they suffered a defeat. This location thus served a dual rolefirst as a gathering point for their political and strategic activities, and later as the scene of a critical armed confrontation. The defeat at St Charles marked a significant setback for the Patriotes, underscoring the risks they faced in their struggle. Despite the loss, the events at St Charles remain a key reference point in their history, illustrating both their resolve and the challenges they encountered.</data>
      <data key="d8">ST CHARLES</data>
    </edge>
