    <edge source="TEPPICH" target="NESBIT" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nesbit and Teppich are two individuals whose interactions are documented in two separate instances, both of which suggest a close and physically engaged relationship. In the first description, during a dinner event, Nesbit pulls Teppich down, an action that indicates a direct physical interaction and implies a level of familiarity or intimacy between them, possibly as friends, partners, or family members. The second description places Teppich at a pagoda, where they see Nesbit as part of a larger group, indicating that both are present in the same social setting and that Teppich is aware of Nesbits presence among others. Together, these descriptions paint a picture of two people who share a social circle and engage in direct, physical contact, suggesting a bond that is both personal and observable within a group context. There are no contradictions between the two accounts; rather, they complement each other by showing different momentsone during a meal and another at a scenic locationwhere their connection is evident. The exact nature of their relationship (e.g., romantic, familial, or platonic) is not specified, but the physical act of pulling down during dinner, combined with mutual awareness in a group setting, points to a dynamic that is both casual and significant. No further details about their backgrounds, roles, or the broader context of the events are provided, so the summary remains focused on their observed interactions.</data>
      <data key="d8">NESBIT</data>
    </edge>
