    <edge source="MOROCCO" target="GREAT BRITAIN" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">MOROCCO and GREAT BRITAIN share a long-standing relationship characterized by formal political and commercial ties, which have been codified through a series of treaties. These treaties establish the legal and diplomatic framework governing their interactions, covering areas such as trade, mutual recognition, and bilateral cooperation. The relationship is historically rooted, with both nations maintaining continuous diplomatic engagement and economic exchanges. While the descriptions emphasize the existence of treaties, they do not specify the exact dates or scope, but collectively they confirm that the two countries have institutionalized their relations through binding agreements. No contradictions exist between the descriptions; rather, they reinforce the same core fact: Great Britain and Morocco have formalized their political and commercial connections via treaties. This enduring partnership reflects a mutual interest in stable diplomatic channels and economic collaboration, likely evolving over time to address changing regional and global circumstances. The treaties serve as the cornerstone of their bilateral relationship, ensuring predictability and mutual benefit in their interactions.</data>
      <data key="d8">GREAT BRITAIN</data>
    </edge>
