    <edge source="ST EUSTACHE" target="REBELLION OF 1837" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">St. Eustache was a significant site during the Rebellion of 1837, a pivotal uprising in Lower Canada (present-day Quebec). The rebellion, which sought political reform and greater local autonomy, culminated in a decisive battle at St. Eustache. This battle marked one of the final and most violent confrontations of the insurgency, where British troops and loyalist volunteers clashed with Patriote rebels. The engagement at St. Eustache resulted in heavy casualties and the burning of the village, effectively quelling the rebellion in the region. As such, St. Eustache is historically recognized as a key battleground and a symbol of the broader struggle for democratic rights and national identity in 19th-century Canada.</data>
      <data key="d8">ST EUSTACHE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ST EUSTACHE" target="MONTREAL" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
