    <edge source="SIR JOHN COLBORNE" target="PATRIOTES" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Sir John Colborne was a British military commander who played a central role in suppressing the Lower Canada Rebellion of 18371838. As the leading loyalist figure, he commanded the British forces tasked with confronting and defeating the Patriotes, a group of insurgents seeking political reform and greater autonomy for French-speaking Canadians. Colborne's primary objective was to crush the rebellion, and he specifically targeted the Patriotes' stronghold at St. Eustache, where he led loyalist troops in a decisive assault to disperse their gatherings and end their organized resistance. His actions were part of a broader British strategy to maintain colonial authority and quell the uprising. Colborne's leadership was marked by a firm, military approach, and he is remembered as the principal British commander opposing the Patriotes throughout the conflict. His campaign culminated in the defeat of the insurgents, restoring British control over the region.</data>
      <data key="d8">SIR JOHN COLBORNE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SIR JOHN COLBORNE" target="BRITISH TROOPS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
