    <edge source="FRENCH CANADIANS" target="PATRIOTES" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">French Canadians were closely associated with the Patriotes, a political and reform movement in the early 19th century. The Patriotes primarily represented the interests of French Canadians, advocating for their rights, political representation, and greater autonomy within the British colonial system. This association was central to the movement's identity, as it sought to address grievances related to governance, language, and cultural preservation. The Patriotes drew significant support from French Canadian communities, particularly in Lower Canada, where they pushed for democratic reforms and opposed the dominance of the British colonial elite. Their efforts ultimately culminated in the Rebellions of 18371838, which were suppressed, but the movement left a lasting impact on French Canadian national identity and political consciousness.</data>
      <data key="d8">FRENCH CANADIANS</data>
    </edge>
