    <edge source="THOMAS STORROW BROWN" target="MONTREAL" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Thomas Storrow Brown was an iron-merchant and hardware businessman based in Montreal. He was active in the city during a period of civil unrest, during which he sustained injuries as a result of rioting that occurred there. Following this incident, Brown returned to Montreal and resumed his hardware business, indicating his continued professional and personal ties to the city. His career in Montreal reflects both his commercial role as a merchant and his presence during turbulent local events.</data>
      <data key="d8">MONTREAL</data>
    </edge>
