    <edge source="COUSIN CSAR" target="ARKANSAS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Cousin Csar is a key figure in the legal and logistical proceedings surrounding the Simon estate, which are centered in the state of Arkansas. He is directly involved in the estates legal contest, indicating his role as a participant or claimant in the dispute. Additionally, Cousin Csar arranged for the remains of the deceased to be transported to Arkansas, suggesting he holds authority or responsibility over the final disposition of the body. These actions place him at the heart of both the jurisdictional and personal matters tied to the estate, with Arkansas serving as the primary location for both the legal battle and the burial arrangements.</data>
      <data key="d8">ARKANSAS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DON CARLO" target="ARKANSAS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Don Carlo, a figure associated with the American frontier, was granted a land title by the Governor of Arkansas to establish a wood yard, indicating his role as a legitimate landholder and entrepreneur in the region. However, his life came to a tragic end, as he was found dead in a saloon in Arkansas following these events. The circumstances surrounding his death are not detailed, but the sequence suggests that after securing his business venture, Don Carlo met with a fatal incident in a local drinking establishment. Thus, his story encompasses both a formal start in the territory through official land rights and a violent or untimely conclusion, leaving his wood yard venture unfulfilled.</data>
      <data key="d8">ARKANSAS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="S. S. SIMON" target="ARKANSAS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">S. S. Simon left a large estate in Arkansas.</data>
      <data key="d8">ARKANSAS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YOUNG SIMON" target="ARKANSAS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Young Simon, a resident of Arkansas, is the central figure in the provided details. According to the descriptions, Simon was from Arkansas, and after his death, his remains were intended to be transported back to Arkansas for burial. Specifically, his body was to be laid to rest beside his father on the familys home plantation. This indicates that Simon had familial ties to a plantation in Arkansas, where his father was already buried, and that his final wish or the arrangement made for him was to be interred there. The two descriptions are complementary, with the first establishing his origin and the second detailing the planned final disposition of his remains. Together, they paint a clear picture of Simons connection to Arkansas as both his home and his intended final resting place, emphasizing the importance of family and place in his life and death.</data>
      <data key="d8">ARKANSAS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CAESAR SIMON" target="ARKANSAS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
