    <edge source="BRACKETT'S BATTALION" target="FORT HENRY" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">BRACKETT'S BATTALION, a military unit, was ordered to proceed to FORT HENRY, Tennessee, in February 1862. This movement was part of the battalion's operational deployment during the American Civil War, as it was directed to reinforce or support the garrison at the fort. The order, issued in that month, placed the battalion at Fort Henry, a key Confederate stronghold on the Tennessee River, which was strategically important for controlling river traffic and regional supply lines. The battalion's arrival at Fort Henry occurred in the context of the broader Union campaign to capture the fort, which ultimately fell to Union forces later that same month. No further details are provided regarding the battalion's specific actions, strength, or subsequent movements, but the order to Fort Henry in February 1862 is the sole documented event in this summary.</data>
      <data key="d8">BRACKETT'S BATTALION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRACKETT'S BATTALION" target="BENTON BARRACKS" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">BRACKETT'S BATTALION was ordered to report at BENTON BARRACKS, located in Missouri (Mo.). This directive applied to the entire battalion, which was instructed to proceed to the military installation known as Benton Barracks for duty or assignment. The order was issued as a formal command, and the battalion was expected to comply by moving to that specific post. Benton Barracks served as the designated rendezvous point for the unit. No further details are provided regarding the timing, purpose, or subsequent actions of the battalion after reporting. The information is consistent across both descriptions, with no contradictions. The battalion's designation and the location of the barracks are the key facts, and the order to report is the central action. The entity names are BRACKETT'S BATTALION and BENTON BARRACKS, and the summary confirms the battalion's obligation to report to that Missouri-based barracks.</data>
      <data key="d8">BRACKETT'S BATTALION</data>
    </edge>
