    <edge source="SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN SUPPLEMENT" target="SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Scientific American Supplement is a supplementary publication issued in conjunction with the main periodical, Scientific American. The two are published together, and they are offered to subscribers at a combined subscription rate, meaning that the Supplement is not sold separately but as part of a bundled subscription with its parent magazine. As a supplement, it extends the content and coverage of Scientific American, providing additional material to readers who subscribe to both. The relationship is integral: the Supplement exists solely as an adjunct to Scientific American, and the combined offering reflects their shared publication and subscription structure.</data>
      <data key="d8">SCIENTIFIC AMERICAN</data>
    </edge>
