    <edge source="EGYPT" target="CHINA" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">China and Egypt share a deep historical connection through their early use of fingerprints for identification and signatures. Both civilizations independently developed practices of using finger marks, with Egypt providing the earliest known evidence of such practices. China also has a long tradition of using fingerprints, though its documented evidence appears later than Egypt's. The comparison between the two nations highlights their parallel yet distinct developments in this area, with Egypt's evidence predating China's. Together, they represent two of the earliest known cultures to employ fingerprinting for personal and legal purposes, underscoring a shared human innovation across ancient societies.</data>
      <data key="d8">EGYPT</data>
    </edge>
