    <edge source="MULEY ABD ERRAHMAN" target="MOGADOR" id="0">
      <data key="d5">related_to</data>
      <data key="d6">1.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Muley Abd Errahman, a monarch of Morocco, had a formative early career that connected him to the coastal city of Mogador (modern-day Essaouira). Although his later role as a sovereign was not directly tied to Mogador, his time there was a crucial part of his preparation for leadership. Specifically, Muley Abd Errahman was appointed administrator of customs in Mogador during his early life. This position served as a practical education in governance, economics, and administrative responsibility, equipping him with the skills and experience necessary for his eventual rule over Morocco. Thus, while Mogador was not the center of his reign, it played a significant role in shaping the future monarch.</data>
      <data key="d8">MOGADOR</data>
    </edge>
